		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 96847222-0886-4086-852e-2cf5385563cb</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Authentication</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">6.2.2026::13:15:43</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::13:15:43</_modifiedTime>
			<_body type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1250\deff0\deflang1045{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset238{\*\fname Arial;}Arial CE;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs20 Authentication\par%0D
\par%0D
Authentication consists of entering 4 digits and comparing them with the password\par%0D
}%0D
</_body>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 1ed7062e-4328-48b8-9098-93b8cbddb054</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Collision detection</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">6.2.2026::13:13:17</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::13:13:17</_modifiedTime>
			<_body type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1250\deff0\deflang1045{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset238 MS Shell Dlg;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset238{\*\fname Arial;}Arial CE;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs17 Collision detection\par%0D
\par%0D
\f1\fs20 Collision detection should take place in each period\par%0D
(iteration) of the gate movement and consists in\par%0D
counting the infrared receiver pulses sent by the\par%0D
infrared transmitter.\par%0D
\par%0D
1. If the number of pulses received and sent differ\par%0D
   significantly, the appropriate signal to the Controller,\par%0D
   which should stop the drive.\par%0D
2. Otherwise, keep moving.\par%0D
}%0D
</_body>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID f3b93fd5-1318-4e44-8384-d60a7b2c45d9</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Firmware</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">6.2.2026::11:59:5</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::11:59:5</_modifiedTime>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 534376e6-fb30-4ed7-afbc-2c631c6d5d09</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Movement</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">6.2.2026::13:11:18</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::13:11:18</_modifiedTime>
			<_body type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1250\deff0\deflang1045{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset238{\*\fname Arial;}Arial CE;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs20 Movement\par%0D
\par%0D
The transition to the gate movement in the given\par%0D
direction requires the following steps:\par%0D
\par%0D
1. Turn on the collision detection.\par%0D
2. Optional activation of the signaling lamp.\par%0D
3. Turning on the gate drive.\par%0D
\par%0D
During the movement taking place in a given\par%0D
direction, the following actions should be repeated\par%0D
every fixed period of time:\par%0D
\par%0D
1. Send a signal about the last traveled distance to\par%0D
   the Controller.\par%0D
2. Check the occurrence of a collision and if the\par%0D
   collision detector signals it, stop the gate movement.\par%0D
3. If the signaling option is active, flash the lamp.\par%0D
}%0D
</_body>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 4eb4ceaa-9a7a-44ec-8bfa-b9386fefb327</_id>
